/*  Shared constants — a `permanently` the hoist reaches, kept as a C global and set where its `Define`
    stands.

    ★ It lives with the program, whatever rabbit its line is in: what the line makes is sent to the
      program's arena, and a rabbit it takes text from is kept, as `regions.cufe` keeps one whose own
      values are stored outside it. One the checker marked `OfItsBlock` is no global: an ordinary name
      of its block, which no function reads.

    ★ A function may be called above the line that gives a constant it reads its value. C would hand
      it a zero, or a NULL series to follow, so the read stops first, as the interpreter does: a flag
      beside the constant, which its line sets. The read asks whether `&cv_k` IS the constant, so a
      local of the same name, or a copy a closure took, is never asked about.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    /// Whether a `Define` of the hoist is a shared constant, and not its block's own.
    Bind fact to is-shared-define, given (the node statement):
        If statement's kind is not "DefineStatement" or (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s word is not "true", return false.
        Define place as cast keyed-field on (statement, ":Place").
        If place is void, return true.
        Return place's word is not "OfItsBlock".
    Done.

    /// The kind of a shared constant: as declared, as the checker noted it where the value reads a name
    /// of its block, or worked out.
    Bind text or failure to constant-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) is false:
            Return cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 7)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define noted as cast keyed-field on (statement, ":ConstantType").
        If noted is not void, return cast one's kind-of-type on (noted) or pass the failure off.
        Return cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// Working this value out can run no body of the program's.
    Bind fact to calls-nothing, given (the node value):
        Define kind as value's kind.
        If kind is "NumberLiteral" or kind is "StringLiteral" or kind is "BooleanLiteral" or kind is "BitsLiteral"
                or kind is "LambdaLiteral" or kind is "AxiomLiteral" or kind is "VariableReference":
            Return true.
        Done.
        If kind is "UnaryExpression", return cast calls-nothing on (cast field-of on (value, 2)).
        If kind is "SeriesLiteral":
            For each element in (cast field-of on (value, 1))'s children, repeat:
                If cast calls-nothing on (element) is false, return false.
            Done.
            Return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// Notes each constant no body can be called ahead of — those from the top down to the first line
    /// that could call one — and says whether that line has not been met yet.
    Bind fact to note-first-constants unto emitter, given (the series of node statements):
        For each statement in statements, repeat:
            Define kind as statement's kind.
            If cast declares-only on (statement), skip.
            If kind is "DefineStatement":
                If cast calls-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) is false, return false.
                If cast is-shared-define on (statement):
                    In one's inferred, the entry for "const-safe:{cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1))}" becomes "yes".
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise if kind is "PullStatement" or kind is "PullRabbitStatement":
                If cast one's note-first-constants on ((cast field-of on (statement, 2))'s children) is false, return false.
            Done.
            Otherwise, return false.
        Done.
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// Whether reading a constant here has to ask if it has a value.
    Bind fact to asks-given unto emitter, given (the text name):
        If (the entry for "const-line:{name}" in one's inferred) is void, return false.
        If (the entry for "const-safe:{name}" in one's inferred) is not void, return false.
        Return (the entry for "%given:{name}" in one's kinds) is void.
    Done.

    Bind c-language axiom to given-asked unto emitter, given (the text name, the number at-row):
        Define given-on as (the entry for "const-line:{name}" in one's inferred but void is "0") converted to number but void is 0.
        Define c-language asked, given (the term held, the term at, the term flag, the text name, the number at-row, the number given-on),
            as [cufet_not_given((void*)&the held == the at && !the flag, the name, the at-row, the given-on)].
        Return asked on (cast c-name on (name), "cvat_{cast c-ident on (name)}", "cvon_{cast c-ident on (name)}", name, at-row, given-on).
    Done.

    /// A shared constant read: its name, stopping first if it has no value yet.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-constant unto emitter, given (the text name, the number at-row):
        If cast one's asks-given on (name) is false, return c-word on (cast c-name on (name)).
        Define c-language read-asked, given (the c-language axiom asked, the term held), as [(*(the asked, &the held))].
        Return read-asked on (cast one's given-asked on (name, at-row), cast c-name on (name)).
    Done.

    /// The constants a body written here reads, asked of as it is made: it takes them along, so they
    /// have to be there. C to run first, or no C at all.
    Bind c-language axiom to constants-asked unto emitter, given (the node body, the map from text to fact own, the number at-row):
        Define found as a map from text to fact.
        Cast one's constants-read on (body, own, found).
        Define names as a series of text.
        For each pair in found, insert the key of pair into names.
        Define c-language asked-too, given (the c-language axiom earlier, the c-language axiom asked), as [the earlier the asked;].
        Define asking as cast no-c.
        For each name in names sorted, repeat:
            If cast one's asks-given on (name), the asking becomes asked-too on (asking, cast one's given-asked on (name, at-row)).
        Done.
        Return asking.
    Done.

    Bind void to constants-read unto emitter, given (the node tree, the map from text to fact own, the map from text to fact found):
        If tree's kind is "VariableReference":
            Define read as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)).
            If (the entry for read in own) is void and (the entry for read in one's kinds) is void and (the entry for read in one's constants) is not void:
                In found, the entry for read becomes true.
            Done.
            Return.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast one's constants-read on (child, own, found).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A shared constant set, where its `Define` stands.
    Bind void or failure to emit-constant unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define shared-kind as the entry for name in one's constants but void is "".
        Define value as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define sent-out as cast keyed-field on (statement, ":Place") is not void.
        If sent-out:
            If cast one's reaches-deeper on (value, 0), cast one's keep-rabbits-below on (0).
            Define c-language override-held, given (the c-language axiom arena), as [{ int cf_ov = cufet_alloc_override; cufet_alloc_override = the arena;].
            Cast one's put on (override-held on (cast arena-at on (0))).
        Done.
        Cast one's put on (assigned-to on (c-word on (cast c-name on (name)), cast one's c-of-as on (value, shared-kind) or pass the failure off)).
        If sent-out, cast one's put on ([cufet_alloc_override = cf_ov; }]).
        If (the entry for "const-line:{name}" in one's inferred) is not void and (the entry for "const-safe:{name}" in one's inferred) is void:
            Cast one's put on (assigned-to on (c-word on ("cvon_{cast c-ident on (name)}"), [1])).
        Done.
        If (the entry for "%main" in one's kinds) is not void, in one's kinds, the entry for "%given:{name}" becomes "yes".
    Done.

    /// A shared constant's C: the global, and the flag its line sets where something may read it sooner.
    Bind text to c-constant-global unto emitter, given (the text name, the text kind):
        Define global as "static {cast c-type on (kind)} {cast c-name on (name)};\n".
        If (the entry for "const-line:{name}" in one's inferred) is void or (the entry for "const-safe:{name}" in one's inferred) is not void, return global.
        Return "{global}static int cvon_{cast c-ident on (name)}; static void* const cvat_{cast c-ident on (name)} = &{cast c-name on (name)};\n".
    Done.
Done.
